<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Armscor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1968">1968</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Armaments Corporation of South Africa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Armscor, the Armaments Corporation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, is the state arms procurement agency established in 1968 to make South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> self-sufficient in weapons under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> arms embargo. Through its subsidiaries it built a large domestic arms industry, producing artillery, armoured vehicles and aircraft, and it was involved in the secret nuclear weapons programme dismantled around 1990–1991.</p></div>
